{
  "title": "FRS 1984-02-10",
  "url": "https://fridayrockshow.fandom.com/wiki/10_February_1984",
  "show": {
    "date": "1984-02-10",
    "comments": [
      "Now a complete show",
      "Tommy says the 38 Special album is 'Tour De France' - somewhat different album that!",
      "Tommy compares Venom to Motorheard, Sex Pistols and Led Zeppelin (in terms of innovation)"
    ]
  },
  "sessions": [
    {
      "artist": "Gary Moore - recorded 27 January 1984 produced by Tony Wilson",
      "details": "Gary Moore (vocals/guitar), Neil Carter (keyboards), Craig Gruber (bass), Ian Paice (drums)"
    },
    {
      "artist": "SNAFU - archive session recorded 28 August 1975 originally broadcast on the Peel show",
      "details": null
    }
  ],
  "track_listing": [],
  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 11.82,
      "end": 27.96,
      "text": "Hello there. Coming up just to 3 minutes past 10, the Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1. Welcome to listeners on VHF in stereo who may have just joined us. If you've tuned from VHF over to stereo, well, I guess it's cleaner. If you can't find any stereo signal, stay with us on mono in medium wave and all that stuff.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.96,
      "end": 32.48,
      "text": "In the next couple of hours, we have Snafu, a good session by them recorded mid-70s,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.84,
      "end": 36.04,
      "text": "Mickey Moody on the guitar, Bobby Harrison on vocals, good singer, that man.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.34,
      "end": 39.26,
      "text": "Also, a brand new session by Gary Moore, and loads of other good stuff.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 39.4,
      "end": 42.62,
      "text": "Stay tuned. It's loud, it's heavy, it starts with ACDC.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.42,
      "end": 47.02,
      "text": "Excellent Southern Boogie merchants they are.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 450.8,
      "end": 454.1,
      "text": "They are 38 Special from their latest album, which is called Tour de France.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 454.22,
      "end": 457.18,
      "text": "It's out on A&M Records. The track was 20th Century Fox.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 457.62,
      "end": 461.36,
      "text": "Before that, ACDC and Highway to Hell, or the album's called Highway to Hell.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 461.36,
      "end": 463.56,
      "text": "The track was, of course, shot down in flames.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 463.72,
      "end": 464.78,
      "text": "It's ten minutes after ten.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 465.22,
      "end": 466.76,
      "text": "Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 466.82,
      "end": 469.66,
      "text": "Played the ACDC track for a chap by the name of Ravi,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 470.2,
      "end": 472.9,
      "text": "whom I'm told has just come out of hospital after having an eye operation,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 473.02,
      "end": 474.98,
      "text": "which I trust was totally successful.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 475.44,
      "end": 477.36,
      "text": "Lots of love from your sister, Bila Sethi.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 478.06,
      "end": 478.96,
      "text": "Hello, Bila, how are you?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 479.1,
      "end": 482.64,
      "text": "And also a mention for Kaz and Louise and Tid and Tosh and Helen,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 483.1,
      "end": 487.26,
      "text": "and also for Rupa, who's been living in India for one year and missing the rock show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 487.92,
      "end": 488.8,
      "text": "Welcome back, Rupa.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 488.8,
      "end": 494.76,
      "text": "Dave from the acid caverns of, where is it, Bradford, MLO,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 494.94,
      "end": 497.4,
      "text": "according to the stamp on the other side of the postcard,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 497.98,
      "end": 502.16,
      "text": "wants to wish B.B. Cole a rotten journey to the Falklands.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 502.44,
      "end": 503.7,
      "text": "It seems he's leaving mid-feb.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 505.16,
      "end": 506.12,
      "text": "Oh, it's a bit mean.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 506.3,
      "end": 508.24,
      "text": "Never know, B.B. Cole might see you down there in June.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 509.06,
      "end": 512.82,
      "text": "And also hello to Zorro and Biz and Stee, I think it is,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 512.82,
      "end": 517.36,
      "text": "one Stee 13% harm to the untrained monkey",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 517.36,
      "end": 520.02,
      "text": "and to marauding psychologists everywhere.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 520.8,
      "end": 523.02,
      "text": "Not forgetting little bits of R.E.F. Enloe",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 523.02,
      "end": 524.38,
      "text": "and the whole of West Yorkshire,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 524.92,
      "end": 528.12,
      "text": "particularly the lower sixths of Sat Grammar School.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 528.66,
      "end": 529.14,
      "text": "Thank you, David.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 530.25,
      "end": 531.87,
      "text": "Mention here to all the bikers and the headbangers",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 531.87,
      "end": 533.11,
      "text": "of St. Colm and Bugle.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 533.39,
      "end": 534.37,
      "text": "Oh, yeah, it says here.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 534.47,
      "end": 536.43,
      "text": "And thanks from Charlie Brown to the following groups.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 536.91,
      "end": 538.59,
      "text": "Saxon, Robert Plant, Scorps, Thizzy,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 538.73,
      "end": 540.89,
      "text": "Finley's your mother, Whitesnake, Slade,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 540.97,
      "end": 543.23,
      "text": "Ozzie, Sammy Hagar, Quo, etc.,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 543.23,
      "end": 545.03,
      "text": "for bothering to take the trouble",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 545.03,
      "end": 547.07,
      "text": "of including Cornwall in their gig tour dates.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 547.07,
      "end": 548.01,
      "text": "and I'm glad that they do.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 550.33,
      "end": 553.05,
      "text": "Right, here's the first bit of excellent music tonight",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 553.05,
      "end": 555.45,
      "text": "from our session by Gary Moore and his new band.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 555.55,
      "end": 556.77,
      "text": "This is Hold On To Love.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 557.53,
      "end": 560.53,
      "text": "A Tokyo Blade.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1056.3,
      "end": 1057.94,
      "text": "That's a track from a four-track 12-incher",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1057.94,
      "end": 1059.94,
      "text": "that's just come out on the Power Station record label.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1060.08,
      "end": 1061.54,
      "text": "It was called Midnight Rendezvous.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1061.66,
      "end": 1063.36,
      "text": "Before that, from our session by Gary Moore,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1064.08,
      "end": 1065.74,
      "text": "his song Hold On To Love.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1067.24,
      "end": 1069.14,
      "text": "Just about 10.21, the Friday Rock Show,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1069.24,
      "end": 1070.38,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1073.69,
      "end": 1076.83,
      "text": "That is from Norbury, London, SW16.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1076.97,
      "end": 1079.45,
      "text": "3AE from Ozzy Osbourne",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1079.45,
      "end": 1082.03,
      "text": "mentioned for",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1082.03,
      "end": 1084.09,
      "text": "some of his mates, the crazy lot of Steve's",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1084.09,
      "end": 1085.93,
      "text": "flat who are John and Mick and Ab",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1085.93,
      "end": 1087.91,
      "text": "I think it isn't Steve, and all the Norbury",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1087.91,
      "end": 1090.09,
      "text": "Edbangers, no H, Murphys",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1090.09,
      "end": 1092.13,
      "text": "and Shirley and",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1092.13,
      "end": 1093.21,
      "text": "Potts and Chris",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1093.21,
      "end": 1096.53,
      "text": "anybody else who happens to be unfortunate to know",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1096.53,
      "end": 1098.41,
      "text": "a crazy female rocker, namely me",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1098.41,
      "end": 1099.83,
      "text": "who calls herself Ozzy Osbourne",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1099.83,
      "end": 1101.87,
      "text": "of Norbury in London",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1101.87,
      "end": 1103.51,
      "text": "big hello to the man",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1103.51,
      "end": 1106.31,
      "text": "who has the name Peter Lutas from",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1106.31,
      "end": 1108.39,
      "text": "Anita. Anita is in",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1108.39,
      "end": 1110.37,
      "text": "Speak in Liverpool. Messages to",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1110.37,
      "end": 1112.07,
      "text": "this fella by the name of Pete. Tell him he's",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1112.07,
      "end": 1114.07,
      "text": "left a very lonely girl at home.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1114.93,
      "end": 1116.55,
      "text": "But not to worry, because I'm going to see him on Sunday.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1117.17,
      "end": 1118.35,
      "text": "Just tell him that I love him",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1118.35,
      "end": 1124.79,
      "text": "a lot. Bit of Texas",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1124.79,
      "end": 1126.51,
      "text": "Boogie from Stevie Ray Vaughan.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1188.13,
      "end": 1189.89,
      "text": "He followed her to school",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1189.89,
      "end": 1193.41,
      "text": "and they broke the teacher's",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1193.41,
      "end": 1197.09,
      "text": "rule. What a time",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1197.09,
      "end": 1200.72,
      "text": "did they have. That day",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1259.49,
      "end": 1263.69,
      "text": "That was Eric Clapton and the Blues",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1435.31,
      "end": 1436.79,
      "text": "Breakers, an ancient track from",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1436.79,
      "end": 1439.13,
      "text": "yonks ago featuring of course Mr. John Mayall",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1439.13,
      "end": 1440.61,
      "text": "included now on the History of Rock",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1440.61,
      "end": 1442.75,
      "text": "Volume 11, it was called Steppin' Out",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1442.75,
      "end": 1445.09,
      "text": "before that Stevie Ray Vaughan and Double Trouble",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1445.09,
      "end": 1446.83,
      "text": "from the album Texas Flood, Mary",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1446.83,
      "end": 1447.79,
      "text": "Had a Little Lamb",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1447.79,
      "end": 1453.95,
      "text": "and that Stevie Ray Vaughan track was",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1453.95,
      "end": 1455.93,
      "text": "actually requested by Mark West",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1455.93,
      "end": 1458.43,
      "text": "of North Highcombe in Lincoln",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1458.43,
      "end": 1460.49,
      "text": "he wants me to say hello",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1460.49,
      "end": 1462.55,
      "text": "around about, well I'm some 12 minutes late",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1462.55,
      "end": 1464.41,
      "text": "now, because he wanted it at",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1464.41,
      "end": 1466.33,
      "text": "10.15, wants me to say hello to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1466.33,
      "end": 1468.17,
      "text": "Chris and also Youngie",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1468.17,
      "end": 1472.63,
      "text": "A.D. Carl Rick, and all the other members of the Chunky Knit Brigade.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1473.05,
      "end": 1473.39,
      "text": "Fine.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1474.07,
      "end": 1476.55,
      "text": "Mark, I've no idea what happened to John Rutzy at all.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1479.68,
      "end": 1482.62,
      "text": "A sad farewell from Richard Bonnell, is it Monnell?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1482.78,
      "end": 1485.28,
      "text": "It is Monnell, M-O-N-E-L-L-E, out of Bristol.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1486.16,
      "end": 1491.8,
      "text": "A really sad farewell here, because it seems he's been in the fourth form of Briz School, B-R-I-Z.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1492.46,
      "end": 1495.44,
      "text": "So it's especially ta-da to Chris, the Kiss fan,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1495.86,
      "end": 1498.38,
      "text": "Penny, the ACDC fan, Jane, the Thin Lizzy fan,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1498.38,
      "end": 1500.92,
      "text": "Nick, the Deo fan, and Matt, the Iron Maiden fan.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1501.0,
      "end": 1503.66,
      "text": "Also, to an ex-headbanger, Ian Hand.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1504.6,
      "end": 1507.0,
      "text": "Richard Monnell, enjoy yourself in your new abode.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1510.04,
      "end": 1512.44,
      "text": "Out of the archives, this band is called Snafu.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1512.6,
      "end": 1513.36,
      "text": "Two tracks by them.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1513.42,
      "end": 1514.72,
      "text": "The first one, Hard to Handle.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1666.17,
      "end": 1672.77,
      "text": "The band used to call themselves Snafu, recorded in the mid-70s.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2006.33,
      "end": 2009.95,
      "text": "Bobby Harrison on the vocals and Mickey Moody on guitar with some other fine musicians as well.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2010.31,
      "end": 2012.39,
      "text": "Two tracks there, Bloodhound and Hard to Handle.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2012.47,
      "end": 2014.35,
      "text": "Two more follow later in the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2014.83,
      "end": 2017.45,
      "text": "It's now 23 minutes before 11 o'clock.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2017.53,
      "end": 2020.51,
      "text": "A quick mention here for a fellow who usually goes to sleep at 10.30.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2020.79,
      "end": 2021.73,
      "text": "Hopefully he's still awake.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2021.89,
      "end": 2025.35,
      "text": "A gentleman by the name of Ian Jones, known to his mates as Budge.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2025.35,
      "end": 2030.99,
      "text": "He says hello to his brother, Daz, and also, Budge, happy birthday for the end of January.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2031.85,
      "end": 2039.05,
      "text": "From the 1980 album called Flush the Fashion, that was Alice Cooper.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2500.34,
      "end": 2501.76,
      "text": "That track was called Pain.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2503.44,
      "end": 2506.52,
      "text": "And it was for a lady who happens to like Alice Cooper, probably not pain,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2506.64,
      "end": 2509.5,
      "text": "a lady by the name of Miss Angela Brown, who lives in Haywood in Lancs.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2510.14,
      "end": 2512.98,
      "text": "Are you Angie? Big fan of Alice Cooper? You are? Me too.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2514.36,
      "end": 2517.38,
      "text": "Also, we'll say we dedicated that to a lady by the name of Kay,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2517.46,
      "end": 2519.14,
      "text": "who is the girlfriend of Chris Dunn.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2519.7,
      "end": 2521.08,
      "text": "His birthday, Feb 12th.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2521.34,
      "end": 2523.16,
      "text": "Happy birthday, Kay, from yourself and Chris.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2523.94,
      "end": 2527.66,
      "text": "And before that, you heard Manowar from their latest album,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2527.76,
      "end": 2529.34,
      "text": "the album which is called Hail to England.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2529.6,
      "end": 2531.02,
      "text": "The track was Killed With Power.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2532.7,
      "end": 2534.02,
      "text": "According to the day sheet in front of me,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2534.08,
      "end": 2535.68,
      "text": "they're going to be touring during March in the UK,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2535.92,
      "end": 2538.2,
      "text": "starting at St. Albans City Hall on March 3rd",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2538.2,
      "end": 2541.62,
      "text": "and ending on the 14th of March at Nottingham Rock City.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2544.27,
      "end": 2545.79,
      "text": "Well-written letter here from Adrian,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2545.97,
      "end": 2550.73,
      "text": "who is the, what, something-something basher of Thetford in Norfolk.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2551.19,
      "end": 2554.15,
      "text": "He wants a mention for all the lads and lasses of Thetford Sixth Form Centre,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2554.15,
      "end": 2556.35,
      "text": "Especially Oz and Mad Mike",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2556.35,
      "end": 2557.97,
      "text": "The Axeman, Iron Horse",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2557.97,
      "end": 2559.53,
      "text": "And The Mutant in Reading",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2559.53,
      "end": 2562.56,
      "text": "Best wishes for a rocking goody",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2562.56,
      "end": 2564.18,
      "text": "1984 to yourself and Tony",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2564.18,
      "end": 2566.62,
      "text": "Thank you, Adrian, the basher",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2566.62,
      "end": 2569.36,
      "text": "And now here's Gary Moore",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2569.36,
      "end": 2572.36,
      "text": "On the good side",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3118.9,
      "end": 3121.48,
      "text": "Gary Moore from our session",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3121.48,
      "end": 3123.7,
      "text": "By him and his new band, Empty Rooms",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3123.7,
      "end": 3125.63,
      "text": "4 minutes to 11",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3125.63,
      "end": 3127.15,
      "text": "It's time for the Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3127.15,
      "end": 3128.65,
      "text": "Last week we played you these tracks",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3128.65,
      "end": 3130.77,
      "text": "From the album Living in Oz",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3130.77,
      "end": 3133.11,
      "text": "Rick Springfield, A Fair of the Heart",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3133.11,
      "end": 3137.81,
      "text": "Granchester Meadows by Pink Floyd from Amagama",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3137.81,
      "end": 3142.41,
      "text": "from the album The Plague, Demon and Black Heath",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3142.41,
      "end": 3147.83,
      "text": "and for the benefit of a few people who wrote in and said what was it",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3147.83,
      "end": 3151.23,
      "text": "the bit of music with all the birds tweeting around in the background",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3151.23,
      "end": 3153.95,
      "text": "was Granchester Meadows by Pink Floyd from Amagama",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3153.95,
      "end": 3158.76,
      "text": "the answer goes like this",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3158.76,
      "end": 3161.29,
      "text": "Brick Spring Field",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3161.29,
      "end": 3165.19,
      "text": "Granchester Meadows and Black Heath",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3166.01,
      "end": 3168.45,
      "text": "Very few people even bother to write in this week.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3169.13,
      "end": 3170.07,
      "text": "In Ignorabria.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3171.47,
      "end": 3173.55,
      "text": "Very few people even bother to have a crack at it.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3173.87,
      "end": 3175.59,
      "text": "And I think only about three people got it right.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3175.71,
      "end": 3178.61,
      "text": "But the champion gets the ten pound record token, twelve pound record token.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3178.73,
      "end": 3179.51,
      "text": "Beg your pardon, David.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3179.95,
      "end": 3183.59,
      "text": "It's David Towle, T-O-W-E-L-L of Hastings in Sussex.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3183.71,
      "end": 3184.35,
      "text": "Well done, sir.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3185.17,
      "end": 3190.57,
      "text": "He says the answer is a piece of ground on which grows wild or tame things such as grass.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3190.57,
      "end": 3195.59,
      "text": "And Mr. Towle actually tells me that he's not going to chuck it in,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3195.67,
      "end": 3198.53,
      "text": "but he considers himself to be an extremely frustrated artist.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3200.09,
      "end": 3201.53,
      "text": "Well, my record token is yours.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3202.07,
      "end": 3203.17,
      "text": "David, good luck with the artwork.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3203.47,
      "end": 3204.51,
      "text": "Nice, nice handwriting.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3204.71,
      "end": 3205.17,
      "text": "It really is.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3205.43,
      "end": 3205.73,
      "text": "Excellent.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3207.56,
      "end": 3210.28,
      "text": "Now, David has put together a Friday Night Connection of his own.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3210.38,
      "end": 3211.04,
      "text": "Three bits of music.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3211.16,
      "end": 3212.42,
      "text": "The Connection is in there somewhere.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3212.68,
      "end": 3215.46,
      "text": "Name of the band, name of the song, album title.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3215.86,
      "end": 3216.46,
      "text": "Who knows?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3216.84,
      "end": 3217.7,
      "text": "You figure it out.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3217.7,
      "end": 3224.3,
      "text": "Friday Night Connection put together by David Towle of Mary's Lane.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3984.17,
      "end": 3986.73,
      "text": "No, Maryland C Road, I think it is.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3987.15,
      "end": 3988.81,
      "text": "Fairlight Hastings in East Sussex.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3988.99,
      "end": 3989.55,
      "text": "Nice one, David.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3989.67,
      "end": 3990.41,
      "text": "Good choice of music.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3994.03,
      "end": 3995.49,
      "text": "Have you any ideas what it is?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3995.55,
      "end": 3996.11,
      "text": "Not you, David.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3996.21,
      "end": 3997.05,
      "text": "You put it together.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3997.23,
      "end": 3997.91,
      "text": "Anybody else?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3998.05,
      "end": 4006.99,
      "text": "If you have any idea what the connection is, then jot it down on a postcard or any form of written communication that you care to employ and send it to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4006.99,
      "end": 4013.89,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection, The Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1, London, W1A4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4013.89,
      "end": 4018.86,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection, The Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1, London",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4018.86,
      "end": 4021.04,
      "text": "W1A4WW",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4021.04,
      "end": 4030.6,
      "text": "We give away once a week a £12 record token",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4030.6,
      "end": 4035.02,
      "text": "And sometimes a t-shirt or anything else we can find in our goodies drawer",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4035.02,
      "end": 4040.3,
      "text": "And don't forget please, put together your own connection as well",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4040.3,
      "end": 4045.7,
      "text": "And their first album which is called The Sentinel",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4583.74,
      "end": 4586.58,
      "text": "Just came out on the Harvest Record label, the track was Cut and Run",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4586.58,
      "end": 4589.78,
      "text": "And the track before that was played off a CD album",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4589.78,
      "end": 4591.08,
      "text": "though it is an actual fact",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4591.08,
      "end": 4592.2,
      "text": "a re-release single",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4592.2,
      "end": 4593.22,
      "text": "by Def Leppard",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4593.22,
      "end": 4594.14,
      "text": "just been re-released",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4594.14,
      "end": 4594.7,
      "text": "on Vertigo",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4594.7,
      "end": 4595.82,
      "text": "is called Photograph",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4595.82,
      "end": 4601.0,
      "text": "it's 11.21",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4601.0,
      "end": 4601.84,
      "text": "communication here",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4601.84,
      "end": 4602.76,
      "text": "from Simon Nudge",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4602.76,
      "end": 4603.3,
      "text": "I think it is",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4603.3,
      "end": 4604.64,
      "text": "at 27 Riverside Road",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4604.64,
      "end": 4605.14,
      "text": "in Oxford",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4605.14,
      "end": 4606.82,
      "text": "please say hello",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4606.82,
      "end": 4608.1,
      "text": "to Kate Mulcair",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4608.1,
      "end": 4609.1,
      "text": "okay I are",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4609.1,
      "end": 4610.12,
      "text": "from Leytonstone",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4610.12,
      "end": 4610.54,
      "text": "in London",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4610.54,
      "end": 4611.14,
      "text": "please tell her",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4611.14,
      "end": 4612.08,
      "text": "that I hope she's doing okay",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4612.08,
      "end": 4613.0,
      "text": "living in the big city",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4613.0,
      "end": 4614.34,
      "text": "and that I'd be really chuffed",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4614.34,
      "end": 4615.02,
      "text": "if she would write",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4615.02,
      "end": 4616.4,
      "text": "and tell me what it's like there",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4616.4,
      "end": 4618.12,
      "text": "oh and tell Kate Mulcair",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4618.12,
      "end": 4619.02,
      "text": "not to get arrested",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4619.02,
      "end": 4620.82,
      "text": "at too many CND marches",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4620.82,
      "end": 4622.08,
      "text": "okay I am",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4622.08,
      "end": 4622.56,
      "text": "Simon",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4622.56,
      "end": 4622.88,
      "text": "okay",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4624.42,
      "end": 4628.96,
      "text": "Every once in a while, a record comes out that has really got a stunning sort of sound.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4629.1,
      "end": 4632.82,
      "text": "And usually, to me, those are records by supremely good musicians,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4633.16,
      "end": 4637.54,
      "text": "or indeed, good musicians who just want to be supremely ear-splitting.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4637.82,
      "end": 4641.58,
      "text": "Like, say, Motorhead when they first started, or the Sex Pistols when they first started,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4641.66,
      "end": 4644.08,
      "text": "even going back to Led Zeppelin and A Whole Lotta Love.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4644.16,
      "end": 4646.74,
      "text": "Well, this record has the same sort of effect on me.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4646.86,
      "end": 4650.44,
      "text": "It's totally and utterly over-the-top, but interesting.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4650.96,
      "end": 4653.82,
      "text": "It's by Venom, and it's called Warhead.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5273.6,
      "end": 5277.2,
      "text": "That, of course, was Blue Oyster Curl from their album Fire of Unknown Origin.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5277.36,
      "end": 5279.28,
      "text": "The track was Veteran of the Psychic Wars.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5279.84,
      "end": 5283.64,
      "text": "Especially for a fellow by the name of James, who has the nickname Clue, C-L-U.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5283.9,
      "end": 5290.04,
      "text": "Got a birthday on the 13th of Feb, and it seems that he listens to this program with his mate Dave from Stockport in Cheshire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5290.6,
      "end": 5293.56,
      "text": "Happy birthday, Clue. From Dave and to both of you, lots of luck.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5295.0,
      "end": 5298.58,
      "text": "Communication here from Pete and Alex, and all the saints and sinners in C-1 House.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5298.58,
      "end": 5301.04,
      "text": "I think it is a Marlborough College, Marlborough in Wiltshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5301.86,
      "end": 5304.14,
      "text": "Dear Tom, our mate Martin Westall has just left school.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5304.26,
      "end": 5307.3,
      "text": "He's continuing his A-levels at a comprehensive in Cirencester.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5307.5,
      "end": 5311.54,
      "text": "As he doesn't have to be in bed on time anymore, please play something after the booze has shut.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5311.88,
      "end": 5314.98,
      "text": "Most of them should have shut by now, unless you're in the middle of the country, you lucky lot.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5315.54,
      "end": 5318.28,
      "text": "P.S. A message here, once again, to Martin.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5318.84,
      "end": 5320.72,
      "text": "It's from those saints and citizens, C-1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5320.82,
      "end": 5322.64,
      "text": "The crick seems empty without you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5323.1,
      "end": 5324.2,
      "text": "See you at the house play.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5324.34,
      "end": 5328.24,
      "text": "Good luck, mate, and don't overdo it on the wine, women, and songs, if any.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5328.24,
      "end": 5333.34,
      "text": "listen to this program but never think of doing that and before that you heard venom totally over",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5333.34,
      "end": 5338.16,
      "text": "the top record but i like it it's out on neat records it's a single or three track 12 inch",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5338.16,
      "end": 5348.96,
      "text": "and in actual fact the track you heard was warhead back to snafu this is lock key snafu",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5836.7,
      "end": 5841.64,
      "text": "out of the archives two tracks by them every little bit hurts and before that you heard lock",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5841.64,
      "end": 5848.6,
      "text": "and key and they made three excuse me three albums between 1973 and 1976 and they were bobby harrison",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5848.6,
      "end": 5850.74,
      "text": "vocals, Mickey Moody on the guitar",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5850.74,
      "end": 5852.96,
      "text": "Pete Sully on keyboards, Colin Gibson on the bass",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5852.96,
      "end": 5854.4,
      "text": "Terry Popple on the drums",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5854.4,
      "end": 5856.34,
      "text": "nice archive session from them",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5856.34,
      "end": 5858.88,
      "text": "good luck to Mickey Moody in whatever he's up to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5858.88,
      "end": 5861.02,
      "text": "I think he's putting a new band together now he's left Whitesnake",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5861.02,
      "end": 5862.86,
      "text": "good luck, this is Gary Moore",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5862.86,
      "end": 5864.78,
      "text": "this incident is going to be his next single as well",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5864.78,
      "end": 5866.1,
      "text": "it's from our session by him",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5866.1,
      "end": 5872.1,
      "text": "from his latest album, just come out on the Atlantic",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6332.81,
      "end": 6334.81,
      "text": "record label, the album is called Penetration",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6334.81,
      "end": 6336.75,
      "text": "the track was entitled Go Down Fighting",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6336.75,
      "end": 6338.63,
      "text": "and before that, the final number",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6338.63,
      "end": 6340.93,
      "text": "by our session, or rather by Gary Moore from our session",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6341.43,
      "end": 6342.83,
      "text": "which is an excellent session, I think.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6342.91,
      "end": 6345.73,
      "text": "It was Shapes of Things, the studio version of what is going to be his next single.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6345.87,
      "end": 6347.27,
      "text": "Gary Moore's band at the moment are",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
